            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $u=4^x$, so $16^x=(4^x)^2=u^2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}u^2-7u-18&=0\\\\(u-9)(u+2)&=0\\\\u&=9\\text{ or }-2\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $4^x>0$, reject $u=-2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}4^x&=9\\\\x\\ln4&=\\ln9\\\\x&=\\frac{\\ln9}{\\ln4}\\\\x&=\\frac{\\ln3}{\\ln2}\\\\x&=\\log_2 3\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
